message: "If you use the Planning Benchmark in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Planning Benchmark: measuring stale regulatory figures in AI financial-advice systems"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "WealthSchema (Capstera)"
    website: "https://www.wealthschema.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/decisionsynth/planning-benchmark"
url: "https://www.wealthschema.com/benchmark"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-31
keywords:
  - llm evaluation
  - benchmark
  - financial planning
  - tax figures
  - stale figure rate
  - synthetic data
abstract: >-
  An open evaluation for AI financial-advice systems measuring figure
  currency: 50 open-split tasks (rule-grounding and threshold/cliff) whose
  answer keys cite primary-source-verified U.S. regulatory figures and
  enumerate the wrong-but-plausible stale values (forbidden figures) with
  reason codes, enabling fully mechanical scoring of the Stale Figure Rate
  alongside pass@1 and pass^k. Accompanied by a dependency-free scorer, a
  pre-registered pilot of record (four systems from three labs, 29% of
  figure-bearing attempts citing a stale or fabricated figure), and a
  contrast run showing zero stale figures when a live cited-figures feed is
  supplied in context. Adversarial and decision-recall families plus a
  held-out reserve are withheld to keep the maintainer-run scoreboard
  re-runnable.
